//RS //! Golden tests: every example program must pass the front end, and (when
//RS //! rustc is available) build and print exactly its expected output.
//RS //! Examples are the executable spec (invariant I5).
//RS //!
//RS //! Also enforces:
//RS //!   I1 — generated code never contains `unsafe`
//RS //!   I2 — rustc accepting the generated code; a rejection here is a
//RS //!        front-end soundness bug, reported loudly
