//RS /// Keep golden's per-run program and FFI-bridge caches private to this test
//RS /// process. Those caches are not content-verified end to end, and parallel test
//RS /// binaries can delete or republish their artifacts while a release example is
//RS /// linking them. Golden examples must prove generated code, not depend on
//RS /// another suite's cache timing.
//RS ///
//RS /// The runtime rlib cache is deliberately NOT in here: it is content-addressed
//RS /// and digest-verified, so it is safe to share and expensive to rebuild.
